    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0287" n="257" xml:id="pg257"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 2.</note>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Bancroft to Mr.
                        Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 249.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-07-29"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            29, 1871</date>. (Received August 18.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: This day, at a quarter before 1, I took the
                    British chargé in my carriage to the Foreign Office, where we delivered
                    simultaneously formal notes, identical in terms, addressed to Prince Bismarck,
                    chancellor of the empire, requesting the German Emperor to accept the office of
                    Arbiter on the northwestern boundary question, under the treaty of Washington. I
                    annex a copy of the note.<seg type="margin">Joint notes presented to the German
                        Government.</seg></p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
